Hi,

As suggested to me by a few people at the first Capital Area SELinux 
Users Group meeting last month I have setup a Wiki for SElinux 
resources that can be maintained by the community.

I started the pages off with two pages of resources on Policy tools and 
General Links. They are really basic but they give a bit of a starting 
point. Some additional links to Tresys's policy tools and presentations 
have already been added by other people after the initial announcement.

Feel free to add any SELinux related content you would like to the wiki 
pages. They are easy to edit so it only takes  a couple minutes to 
share some useful links or tips and everyone can benefit from them.

Anyone can edit the content of the pages after creating an account 
(just click the "User Preferences" link in the upper right corner of 
any page). If you havn't used a Wiki before, I'd suggest looking at a 
few of the links at the bottom of the first page and the documentation 
under the "HelpContents" link at the top of the page.

If you have any technical problems with the site, please contact me. If 
you have ideas or questions about content -- just go ahead and add them 
directly to the site, or ask your questions in the comment fields you 
can append to pages. That way everyone can participate.

Cheers,

Jonathan

